<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.12.7: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00275</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.12.7: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>44de000a-51c3-44ec-9b8c-9dcab516cdf7</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
      <para>In 1 - 2, find the equation of a line with given slope and \( y \)-intercept. Write the equation in slope-intercept form.</para>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise data-content-id="8ef284c1-00ab-48a5-88e3-a507f9d890c1" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>slope 3 and \( y \)-intercept \( ( 0,5) \)</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(y=5x+3\)</para>
            <para>\(y=3x+0\)</para>
            <para>\(y=3x+5\)</para>
            <para>\(y=0x+3\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \( y=3x+5 \) 
        \(\begin{array}{rcl}y-y_1&amp;=&amp;m(x-x_1)\\y-(5)&amp;=&amp;3(x-(0))\\y-5&amp;=&amp;3(x)\\y-5&amp;=&amp;3x\\y&amp;=&amp;3x+5\\&amp;&amp;\end{array}\)
        \(\begin{array}{rcl}y-y_1&amp;=&amp;m(x-x_1)\\y-(5)&amp;=&amp;3(x-(0))\\y-5&amp;=&amp;3(x)\\y-5&amp;=&amp;3x\\y&amp;=&amp;3x+5\\&amp;&amp;\end{array}\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.12.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(y=3x+5\). </para>
            <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y-y_1&amp;=&amp;m(x-x_1)\\y-(5)&amp;=&amp;3(x-(0))\\y-5&amp;=&amp;3(x)\\y-5&amp;=&amp;3x\\y&amp;=&amp;3x+5\\&amp;&amp;\end{array}\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="d44ab61a-84e5-4c4c-822b-3016c0730bf5" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>slope \(−3 \) and \( y \)-intercept \( (0,−1)\)</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(y=-x-3\)</para>
            <para>\(y=-3x-1\)</para>
            <para>\(y=-x+0\)</para>
            <para>\(y=0x-3\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \( y=-3x-1 \)</para>
            <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y-y_1&amp;=&amp;m(x-x_1)\\y-(-1)&amp;=&amp;-3(x-(0))\\y+1&amp;=&amp;-3(x)\\y+1&amp;=&amp;-3x\\y&amp;=&amp;-3x-1\end{array}\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.12.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(y=-3x-1\). </para>
            <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y-y_1&amp;=&amp;m(x-x_1)\\y-(-1)&amp;=&amp;-3(x-(0))\\y+1&amp;=&amp;-3(x)\\y+1&amp;=&amp;-3x\\y&amp;=&amp;-3x-1\end{array}\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="22534ea5-e0df-44bb-82b5-d457a01de3a3" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>In 3 - 4, Choose the slope-intercept form of the equation of the line, shown in each graph.</para>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="">
                  <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_01_14_16_01.png"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
            </para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(y=-3x+5\)</para>
            <para>\(y=5x-3\)</para>
            <para>\(y=-5x+3\)</para>
            <para>\(y=3x-5\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \( y=3x-5 \)</para>
            <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}m&amp;=&amp;\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{(1)-(-2)}{(2)-(1)}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{1+2}{2-1}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{3}{1}=3\end{array}\)</para>
            <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y−y_1&amp;=&amp;m(x−x_1)\\y−(−2)&amp;=&amp;3(x−(1))\\y+2&amp;=&amp;3(x−1)\\y+2&amp;=&amp;3x−3\\y&amp;=&amp;3x−5\end{array}\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.12.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(y=3x-5\). </para>
            <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}m&amp;=&amp;\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{(1)-(-2)}{(2)-(1)}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{1+2}{2-1}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{3}{1}=3\end{array}\)</para>
            <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y−y_1&amp;=&amp;m(x−x_1)\\y−(−2)&amp;=&amp;3(x−(1))\\y+2&amp;=&amp;3(x−1)\\y+2&amp;=&amp;3x−3\\y&amp;=&amp;3x−5\end{array}\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="b4b0e8cb-bca8-4efe-860f-165f82fd0d0f" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>
              <figure>
                <media alt="">
                  <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_01_14_16_02.png"/>
                </media>
              </figure>
            </para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(y=-2x+4\)</para>
            <para>\(y=2x+4\)</para>
            <para>\(y=\frac12x -4\)</para>
            <para>\(y=\frac12 x+2\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \( y=-2x+4 \)</para>
            <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}m&amp;=&amp;\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{(4)-(0)}{(0)-(2)}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{4-0}{0-2}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{4}{-2}&amp;=&amp;-2\end{array}\)</para>
            <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y − y_1 &amp;=&amp; m(x − x_1)\\y − (0) &amp;=&amp; −2(x − (2))\\y &amp;=&amp; −2(x − 2)\\y &amp;=&amp; −2x + 4\end{array}\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.12.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(y=-2x+4\). </para>
            <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}m&amp;=&amp;\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{(4)-(0)}{(0)-(2)}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{4-0}{0-2}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{4}{-2}&amp;=&amp;-2\end{array}\)</para>
            <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y − y_1 &amp;=&amp; m(x − x_1)\\y − (0) &amp;=&amp; −2(x − (2))\\y &amp;=&amp; −2(x − 2)\\y &amp;=&amp; −2x + 4\end{array}\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="a0d8a289-e8c3-4a6f-b6aa-febc913fcfa0" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\(m=−7\), point \((−1,−3)\)</para>
            <para>Choose the equation of a line with the given
          slope and containing the given point that best represents the line in
          slope-intercept form. </para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(y=-7x-1\)</para>
            <para>\(y=-7x-3\)</para>
            <para>\(y=-3x+10\)</para>
            <para>\(y=-7x-10\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \( y=-7x-10 \)</para>
            <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y − y_1 &amp;=&amp; m(x − x_1)\\y − (−3) &amp;=&amp; −7(x − (−1))\\y + 3 &amp;=&amp; −7(x + 1)\\y + 3 &amp;=&amp; −7x − 7\\y &amp;=&amp; −7x − 10\end{array}\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.12.2.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(y=-7x-10\). </para>
            <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y − y_1 &amp;=&amp; m(x − x_1)\\y − (−3) &amp;=&amp; −7(x − (−1))\\y + 3 &amp;=&amp; −7(x + 1)\\y + 3 &amp;=&amp; −7x − 7\\y &amp;=&amp; −7x − 10\end{array}\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="988663d2-d0e1-4007-a583-801276ebffbe" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\((0,4)\) and \((2,−3)\)</para>
            <para>Choose the equation of a line containing the given points that best
          represents the line in slope-intercept form. </para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(y=-\frac72x-3\)</para>
            <para>\(y=\frac72x+4\)</para>
            <para>\(y=-\frac27x+4\)</para>
            <para>\(y=-\frac72x+4\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(y=-\frac72x+4\)</para>
            <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}m&amp;=&amp;\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{(-3)-(4)}{(2)-(0)}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{-3-4}{2-0}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{-7}{2}\end{array}\)</para>
            <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y − y_1 &amp;=&amp; m(x − x_1)\\y − (4) &amp;=&amp; -\frac{7}{2}(x − (0))\\y − 4 &amp;=&amp; -\frac{7}{2}(x)\\y &amp;=&amp; -\frac{7}{2}x + 4\end{array}\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.12.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(y=-\frac72x+4\). </para>
            <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}m&amp;=&amp;\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{(-3)-(4)}{(2)-(0)}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{-3-4}{2-0}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{-7}{2}\end{array}\)</para>
            <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y − y_1 &amp;=&amp; m(x − x_1)\\y − (4) &amp;=&amp; -\frac{7}{2}(x − (0))\\y − 4 &amp;=&amp; -\frac{7}{2}(x)\\y &amp;=&amp; -\frac{7}{2}x + 4\end{array}\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="1ddea227-6cfa-401e-9c34-d66382305700" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>\((3,−4)\) and \((5,−4)\)</para>
            <para>Choose the equation of a line containing the given points
          that best represents the line in slope-intercept form.</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(y=-4\)</para>
            <para>\(y=0\)</para>
            <para>\(x=2\)</para>
            <para>\(x=-2\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \(y=-4\)</para>
            <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}m&amp;=&amp;\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{(-4)-(-4)}{(5)-(3)}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{-4+4}{5-3}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{0}{2}=0\end{array}\)</para>
            <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y − y_1 &amp;=&amp; m(x − x_1)\\y − (−4) &amp;=&amp; 0(x − (3))\\y + 4 &amp;=&amp; 0(x − 3)\\y &amp;=&amp; −4\end{array}\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.12.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(y=-4\). </para>
            <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}m&amp;=&amp;\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{(-4)-(-4)}{(5)-(3)}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{-4+4}{5-3}\\m&amp;=&amp;\frac{0}{2}=0\end{array}\)</para>
            <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y − y_1 &amp;=&amp; m(x − x_1)\\y − (−4) &amp;=&amp; 0(x − (3))\\y + 4 &amp;=&amp; 0(x − 3)\\y &amp;=&amp; −4\end{array}\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="0d4df168-9815-422a-b8fe-790cdafe44fc" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which of the following equations is 
          \(y-5=3(x-2)\) written in standard form? </para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(y=3x-1\)</para>
            <para>\(-3x+y = -1 \)</para>
            <para>\(3x - y =1\)</para>
            <para>\(y=3x -11\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}y-5&amp;=&amp;3(x-2)\\y-5&amp;=&amp;3x-6\\y-5+5&amp;=&amp;3x-6+5\\y&amp;=&amp;3x-1\\y-3x&amp;=&amp;3x-3x-1\\-3x +y&amp;=&amp;-1\\\frac{-3x}{ -1}+\frac{y}{-1}&amp;=&amp;{-1}{-1}\\3x - y &amp;=&amp;1\end{array}\)</para>
            <para>Try again. Revisit activity 1.12.4.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(3x - y =1\). </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="c345c099-f334-4829-a6f2-07a7c7ebcf82" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Write the equation of a line that contains the points \((–3,–1)\) and \((2,–2)\). Write the equation in point-slope form.</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(y-2=3(x-4)\)</para>
            <para>\(y-4=-3(x+2)\)</para>
            <para>\(y+2=\frac13(x-4)\)</para>
            <para>\(y-4=3(x-2)\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. </para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(y-2=3(x-4)\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="1793fb44-9898-4e66-9783-3eb4a0f4b282" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Write the equation of a line that contains the point (2, -3) with a slope of 8. Write the equation in standard form.</para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(8x - y = -19 \)</para>
            <para>\(8x + y = 19\)</para>
            <para>\(8x-y=19\)</para>
            <para>\( 19x + y = 8\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. </para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(8x-y=19\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise data-content-id="545e7634-a60f-48dc-aa3e-fc69ccc363d6" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Write the equation of a line that contains the points (3, 1) and (-1, 5). Write the equation in standard form. </para>
            <para>Multiple Choice:</para>
            <para>\(x - y = 4 \)</para>
            <para>\(x+y=4\)</para>
            <para>\(-x+y = 4\)</para>
            <para>\(x + y = -4\)</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct!</para>
            <para>Try again. </para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(x+y=4\)</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
    </section>
  </content>
